{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2085","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Serval and Kaitenzushi Buffet"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Serval has just found a Kaitenzushi buffet restaurant. Kaitenzushi means that there is a conveyor belt in the restaurant, delivering plates of sushi in front of the customer, Serval."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this restaurant, each plate contains exactly $$$k$$$ pieces of sushi and the $$$i$$$-th plate has a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$d_i$$$. Serval will have a meal in this restaurant for $$$n$$$ minutes, and within the $$$n$$$ minutes, he must eat up "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the pieces of sushi he took from the belt."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Denote the counter for uneaten taken pieces of sushi as $$$r$$$. Initially, $$$r=0$$$. In the $$$i$$$-th minute ($$$1\\leq i\\leq n$$$), only the $$$i$$$-th plate of sushi will be delivered in front of Serval, and he can do "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Take the $$$i$$$-th plate of sushi (whose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$d_i$$$) from the belt, and $$$r$$$ will be increased by $$$k$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Eat one uneaten piece of sushi that he took from the belt before, and $$$r$$$ will be decreased by $$$1$$$. Note that you can do this only if $$$r \\gt 0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Or, do nothing, and $$$r$$$ will remain unchanged. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that after the $$$n$$$ minutes, the value of $$$r$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"must"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" be $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Serval wants to maximize the sum of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousnesses"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all the plates he took. Help him find it out!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1\\leq k \\lt n\\leq 2\\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of minutes of the meal and the number of sushi pieces in each plate."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$d_1, d_2, \\ldots, d_n$$$ ($$$1\\leq d_i\\leq 10^9$$$) — the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of each plate."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer — the maximum possible sum of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousnesses"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all the plates Serval took."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n5 2\n3 6 4 1 2\n7 1\n3 1 4 1 5 9 2\n4 3\n4 3 2 1\n6 2\n1 3 5 2 4 6\n6 1\n1000000000 1 1000000000 1 1000000000 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n16\n4\n6\n3000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, it can be shown that Serval can eat up at most one plate of sushi. Since the second plate of sushi has the greatest "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"deliciousness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$6$$$ among all the plates, he will take it from the belt in the second minute, and then eat it up in the following $$$2$$$ minutes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Minute"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$1$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","te